            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0624" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9493/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-15T17:00:00+09:00">May 15, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 15—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. 1. Department’s 80, May 14, 7 p.m. received and decoded today at 3 p.m. I
                    saw the Minister for Foreign Affairs at 3:45 and orally and informally carried
                    out the Department’s instructions.</p>
                <p>2. The Minister informed me that the Counsellor of the British Embassy had this
                    morning advised the Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs that the British
                    Government had likewise decided to raise its Legation in China to the status of
                    an Embassy. No replies have been received from the French or German
                    Governments.</p>
                <p>3. Although all steps have been taken to carry out the decisions of the Japanese
                    Government and although it was intended to make the official announcement
                    tomorrow, the Minister said that he would now withhold the official announcement
                    until Saturday morning May <pb facs="0625" n="513" xml:id="pg513"/> 18 in order
                    to afford the British Government and, in the event of a favorable decision, the
                    American Government an opportunity for simultaneous announcement.</p>
                <p>4. The British Embassy informs me that the announcement of the decision of the
                    British Government will be made simultaneously with that of the Japanese
                    Government.</p>
                <p>5. I shall endeavor tomorrow to ascertain the precise hour of release in Tokyo
                    and to cable the Department.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
